==============================================================================================
PART 2  THE REGULARIZABLE SIDE: the construction's Dedekind sum CLOSES (-> -1/12=zeta(-1))
  s(n,Phi6) = -T/(12T+6),  T=n(n-1)/2;  margin=-12 s/n^2;  n^2*margin -> -12 zeta(-1)=1
==============================================================================================
  n=  6: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.080645  enum True   n^2*margin=0.96774 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  n=  7: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.081395  enum True   n^2*margin=0.97674 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  n= 10: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.082418  enum True   n^2*margin=0.98901 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  n= 14: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.082878  enum True   n^2*margin=0.99454 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  n= 50: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.083299  enum True   n^2*margin=0.99959 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  n=200: s(n,Phi6) closed=-0.083331  (skip enum)   n^2*margin=0.99997 (->1);  Phi6 mod n = 1 (==1 => 1-step reciprocity = AP telescoping)
  => construction is REGULARIZABLE: Phi6==1 mod n makes the AP/interval sawtooth sum telescope
     in one reciprocity step -> closed form -> the -1/12 Eisenstein anomaly.

