PART 3  THE ORDER PARAMETER QUANTIFIES THE RESIDUAL (the open part)
==============================================================================================
  E_norm (order): construction (residues) vs beaters (both at their n):
    n=7: construction E_norm=0.726 (log-concave, Eisenstein) vs beater E_norm=0.753 (disordered, cusp)  M_beater=0.1538
    n=8: construction E_norm=0.740 (log-concave, Eisenstein) vs beater E_norm=0.584 (disordered, cusp)  M_beater=0.1333
    n=9: construction E_norm=0.756 (log-concave, Eisenstein) vs beater E_norm=0.477 (disordered, cusp)  M_beater=0.1212
    n=10: construction E_norm=0.771 (log-concave, Eisenstein) vs beater E_norm=0.673 (disordered, cusp)  M_beater=0.1081
  correlation of beater DISORDER (1-E_norm) with DEPTH (n/Phi6 - M_beater), the residual size:
    n=7: disorder(1-E_norm)=0.247   residual depth(n/Phi6 - M)=0.0089
    n=8: disorder(1-E_norm)=0.416   residual depth(n/Phi6 - M)=0.0070
    n=9: disorder(1-E_norm)=0.523   residual depth(n/Phi6 - M)=0.0021
    n=10: disorder(1-E_norm)=0.327   residual depth(n/Phi6 - M)=0.0018
    Pearson(disorder, residual depth) = -0.551

==============================================================================================
PART 4  WHY ORDER = REGULARIZABLE: interval autocorr = Fejer triangle => Fourier >= 0 (pos-def)
==============================================================================================
  interval size 5: autocorrelation == triangle (m-|t|)_+ ? True  -> Fourier = |hat 1_R|^2 = Fejer kernel >= 0
  interval size 8: autocorrelation == triangle (m-|t|)_+ ? True  -> Fourier = |hat 1_R|^2 = Fejer kernel >= 0
  => the ordered (interval/AP) set has a LOG-CONCAVE (Fejer) autocorrelation and a NON-NEGATIVE
     power spectrum -- positive-definite, hence its Dedekind/sawtooth sum telescopes and
     REGULARIZES (-1/12 = zeta(-1), the E2/Eisenstein anomaly, = the level-k Fejer magic function).
     Disorder breaks log-concavity => no telescoping => cusp/un-regularizable residual.
DONE.
